WEBVTT

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:04.300
Bismillah, alhamdulillah, wassalatu wassalamu ala
rasulullah. Hello calculus students. Today

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:08.220
we're going to be solving related rates with
calculus. Let's get right into our

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:13.390
examples. For our first example, we have here that a
balloon's radius, spherical, grows

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:18.710
at 0 .5 centimeters per second. Find the rate of
change of the surface area when the

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.790
surface area equals 100 pi
centimeters squared.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:28.190
Now, when I was first doing calculus, related
rates was not my favorite unit at the

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:32.810
beginning because I was always worried when I
saw word problems in math. I always

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:37.990
thought I didn't know how to approach it,
so it seemed like a big scary

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.890
question versus the easy calculation
questions. But actually, once I started to

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:45.230
understand what's happening, they became much
easier than the calculation questions

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:50.350
because usually there's much, much less
steps. And your only big step, quote

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:55.270
unquote, is the first initial of figuring out
what you need to use to answer this

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:59.210
question. But to find out what you need to use
is actually very easy once you're

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:04.070
able to identify what you have and what you need
to find out, your givens and your

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:08.270
unknowns. So let's go through these two
sentences here and see if we can identify

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:10.630
what we have and what we need to find out.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:17.050
So first, for what are our givens, a
balloon's radius, spherical,

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:22.870
grows at 0 .5 centimeters per second. In this
first sentence, we already get two

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:28.030
pieces of information because we know it's
spherical, and we know that the

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:30.670
rate of the radius is 0 .5.

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:36.840
How spherical helps us is because that's going
to tell us which shapes equations

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:40.280
we're going to need to use, right? Because
usually for related rates, we're going to

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:44.980
be dealing with different 3D shapes. And these 3D
shapes are going to have their own

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:49.240
respective surface area equations and volume
equations. So here we know we're going

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:52.900
to have to deal with the spheres equations. And
we know already one of the rates

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:54.500
that are going to be relevant
to us when solving.

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:59.980
Now, in the second sentence, it says, find the
rate of change of the surface area

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:04.940
when the surface area equals 100 pi
centimeters squared. And this is

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.560
obviously a given here.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:12.070
And we can also figure out what we need to find
because it literally says, find the

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:15.490
rate of change. So we're going to have to
underline this. But it's not just this

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:19.170
that we're underlining. It's finding the rate
of change of what? Of the surface

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:19.630
area.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:25.790
So under the blue here, we have what we need to
find out. and under the black we

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:31.200
have our givens and now because we know we have
to relate surface area and the

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:36.060
sphere we're going to bring out our surface area
for the sphere equation which is SA

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:41.550
equals 4 pi r squared now a lot of

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:46.710
these surface area area and volume equations
especially for this unit you're going

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:50.470
to have to memorize before going into the
test. But a lot of the time, you can

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:55.770
sometimes get some piece of information
from the question to figure out

00:02:55.620 --> 00:03:00.490
what the power of your variable in the equation
is going to be. What I mean by that

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:04.210
is here we know that our r is most probably
going to be squared, even if I didn't

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:07.610
know this equation, because we know that our
surface area is going to be centimeters

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:11.510
squared, right? So because the centimeter is
squared, and we know r is just going to

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:16.810
be in the single unit, so it's probably
going to be r squared in

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:21.790
our formula for the surface area. Either way,
though, other than this equation, we

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:27.010
also need our rate of change equation. And we
get that equation when we take the

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:32.430
derivative of our surface area with
respect to time. When we take

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:37.290
a derivative with respect to time, that's how
we figure out the change over time.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:41.360
Either way, when we take the derivative with respect to
time here, we're going to be left

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:45.820
with d of SA over dt

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:51.960
equals 4 pi and then

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:56.060
d of r squared over dt.

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:01.730
We don't have to worry about putting a dt under the
4 pi or deriving the 4 pi because

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:02.430
it's a constant.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:08.990
Now, in our next step, we're going to
keep this as dSA over dt.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:16.510
And then we're going to bring down this 4 pi as
a factor. And then we're going to

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:21.990
apply the chain rule here to get d of

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:27.890
r squared over dr times dr

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:33.230
over dt. And this is when we use the
chain rule with the Leibniz

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:38.390
notation. This is how it's going to be
seen. now we can do d of SA

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:43.870
over dt equals 4 pi times

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:48.670
2r dot or times dr over dt

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:49.910
because

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:58.450
here we're able to differentiate r when we're
doing it with respect to r and this is

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:03.490
just our power rule and then we have to multiply
by that ratio of dr over dt because

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:08.130
when we cancel these two out that would be what
we had here earlier, which is our

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:09.390
Leibniz notation, as we already know.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:15.910
Now, it would go 8 pi r dr over

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:16.330
dt.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:22.620
And that is the relationship between
our derivative with respect

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:27.940
to time of our SA and our derivative with
respect to time with our radius. So

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:33.400
this is our rate of change for the surface
area, and this is our rate of change

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:38.710
for the radius. okay so what do we
have from all of these

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:44.130
variables and what do we not have so we are
given SA and this isn't the rate

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:48.830
of SA this is just SA so we know this one this
one is a given so I'm gonna circle

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:54.310
and blue and black our givens in our blue are
unknowns we are also given the

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:58.510
rate of dr over dt so we're given
this right here and

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:05.470
we are asked for the rate of change of the
surface area so we're going to

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:08.730
circle the rate of change of the
surface area, this one, in blue.

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:15.460
Now, the only variable we have left over
between these two equations

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:20.760
is our r. r we have left over in

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:25.480
our non -rate of change equation, and we have
it left over in our rate of change

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:30.500
equation. And because r is going to remain the
same number for both, we can solve

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:35.720
our r in our first equation and then use
that r in the second equation

00:06:35.570 --> 00:06:40.920
with the rest of our known, which is our
dr over dt, to solve for our

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:46.250
dSA over dt. Now, I know that was a lot what I
just said, but it'll make sense as I

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:51.660
go through these steps. So let's
also, for simplicity's sake,

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:56.600
label this as equation one and this as equation
two, so we can easily reference what

00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:56.940
we're doing.

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:00.240
So now we're going to go and
we're going to say

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:02.230
solve

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:06.920
r in first equation.

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:13.410
So here we have SA equals 4 pi r squared.

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:19.160
And we know SA is 100 pi, so we
can do 100 pi equals

00:07:19.010 --> 00:07:24.450
4 pi of r squared. And then we can rearrange
this, have it r squared equals

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:29.950
100 pi over 4 pi, and then we're going to,

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:34.610
these two pi's will cancel out, and then 100
divide up 4 by 25, so it'll be r

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:38.550
squared equals 25, r equals the
square root of 25.

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:45.550
Now because we have our r, we
can, in our second

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:45.990
equation,

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:48.190
solve

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:57.070
d of SA over d of t into

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:58.710
now

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:02.160
using the r that we got.

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:08.790
Now we can now use our r and plug in
both our r and our dr over dt

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:12.950
from the top to solve for our dSA over dt.

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:20.260
So here let's re-put our equation
first we have d SA over

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:25.740
dt equals 8 pi r dr

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:28.020
over dt and

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:34.400
now we can go 8 pi square root of 25

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:39.640
which is what our r is and our dr
over dt which is 0 .5

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:40.620
and

00:08:41.590 --> 00:08:43.900
then we can put all of these
together in our calculator.

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:52.730
8 times pi times the root of 25

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:56.520
times 0 .5.

00:08:57.270 --> 00:09:00.580
And we get as our answer 20 pi.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:05.150
Or if you want to write it
without the pi, just as a

00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:11.090
real number, we can do 62

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:15.350
.831 as our final answer,

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:20.690
but no, not fully as our final answer, sorry. It
is a rate, right? So it's going to

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:25.690
be 62 .831 centimeters squared

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:30.960
per second. And we get the centimeter squared
per second because we know that

00:09:30.810 --> 00:09:36.180
dr over dt is centimeters over s, and we

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:41.560
know that r is centimeters. So if you
multiply the centimeters by the,

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:46.760
if you do centimeters, times
centimeters over s, that

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:52.730
equals centimeters squared over s. So this is
our final answer right here. So this

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:53.830
should have also been centimeters.

00:09:55.210 --> 00:09:57.020
Thank you, and see you in
the next example.
